+# FRO-326 frontend preparation
+
+This change prepares supported Order Details presentation against the current API. It does not complete FRO-326 or activate unavailable contracts. An Order is the backend purchase order; a colli is a permanent handling unit.
+
+## Implemented and preserved
+
+- Existing route query/loading/error/not-found handling and standalone Edit access are retained. Creation and API contracts are unchanged.
+- Overview uses production Card components and a four/two/one-column fact grid. The existing status badge keeps its tone and dot, with larger page-local emphasis and supported lifecycle forms in the status card.
+- One mounted action controller owns command drafts across tabs and language changes. Its lifetime is keyed to Order ID. Successful commands clear only their own draft; failed commands retain it. Command inputs are disabled during submission to prevent newer edits being cleared by the response.
+- Leaving for a different pathname asks before discarding drafts; Stay/Escape retains them. Browser unload protection is enabled while dirty or submitting. Discard is disabled during command submission.
+- Available actions retains the existing reminder command, audited status correction, split and terminal disposition. Split and disposition have independent reasons. The panel stays mounted while hidden so pending reminder state survives tab switches. Comments remain the existing activity-message command in History.
+- Collis use a compact read-only table, stable trace links, separate expansion buttons, terminal badges, existing measurements including net weight, and independent two-column expansions (one column on small screens). Missing measurements remain missing. DG class appears only for DG collis. Existing bonded data is retained without interpreting it as a customs regime.
+- Reminder unavailability uses the existing server reason mapping in a focus/click/hover information popover. The current direct-send behavior remains until FRO-328 supplies reviewed email preparation.
+- AttachmentPanel is unchanged, including authority gates and inherited read-only provenance.
+
+Shared UI additions are opt-in: `TabPanel.keepMounted` and `Modal.ariaLabel`. Other callers preserve their prior behavior.
+
+## Remaining integration owners
+
+FRO-346: atomic/versioned Details and readiness save; FRO-303/356: restricted Invoice company and ALK correction; FRO-333/334/356: explicit Pickup/customs; FRO-292: independently scoped Notes; FRO-337: exact unit-price invoice editor; FRO-294/295/297/332: final colli fields and inline mutations; FRO-328: prepared/idempotent email review; FRO-349/355 with FRO-353/354: Supplier Invoice and Entry Note routes. Retire the old Edit route only after capability parity. Do not emulate these contracts through broad updates or invented fields.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run `npm run test`, `npm run build`, `npm run format:check`, and `npx tsc --noEmit` in this client. Consequential regression tests cover tab/language draft retention, Order-identity reset, discard/Stay, beforeunload, failed correction retry/payload, independent operational reasons, pending input locking, and pending reminder retention. Existing stock, form, route and attachment tests remain in the suite.
+
+Browser validation uses the actual Vite application with a temporary fixture API at localhost, a fixture-only session, and both API environment URLs explicitly pointing to that server. The fixture launcher/configuration and data live outside the production checkout and are not part of application delivery. No live portal request or business-data mutation is needed. Exercise desktop/400px EN/EL, loading/error/not-found/empty, editor/view-only, terminal colli inspection, stock cancellation, failed/pending command behavior and inherited files. Fixtures demonstrate frontend behavior only; they cannot verify backend permissions, concurrency, idempotency or transactionality.
+
+Baseline limitations on the preparation machine: checked-in package manifest and lockfile are inconsistent (`npm ci` fails). Local verification uses `npm install --package-lock=false`, leaving both files unchanged. Node24.13.0/npm11.6.2 were available (repository guidance prefers Node22.13.0). Existing delivery-note test casts prevent a clean typecheck, and existing repository-wide formatting drift prevents a clean format check. These unrelated files are outside this UI change.
+
+## Full UI preparation (approved continuation)
+
+The reusable UI is prepared now, independently of live API activation:
+
+- OrderDetailsNotes: separate Internal/External sections, independent TanStack Form drafts, trim/clear/max length, failure retention and reviewed revisions. Omit the internal prop entirely for external readers; this is not a substitute for server filtering.
+- OrderDetailsEditor: one ordinary or restricted correction session, adapter-supplied field locks/capabilities, review before confirmation, revision invalidation. The adapter must return authoritative fiscal/customs impacts and apply the actual atomic command.
+- OrderEditableRows: independent colli/invoice drafts, copy whitelist, terminal protections, stale operation checks, per-row callbacks and trace navigation callback. UI interfaces are not wire contracts. Generic safe colli persistence ownership remains unresolved.
+- Exact invoice totals use integer decimal arithmetic. No float approximation or invented transport API.
+- OrderReviewedEmails: shared two-location preparation/explicit-send state; context invalidation and retained failures. OrderDocumentAction distinguishes pending/error/denied/create/open; unresolved routes remain navigation callbacks.
+- OrderDetailsPreparedPage composes all six tabs using production primitives. The original route retains working commands until integration parity. It now also displays supported Vessel/Greece/current warehouse/DN/Urgent fields and uses the agreed tab order.
+
+### Local review entry
+
+Run the existing client Vite dev server bound to loopback, then open /dev/fro326/index.html. On this machine it is available at http://127.0.0.1:8341/dev/fro326/index.html.
+
+The entry imports reusable React components and production design primitives. It is DEV + loopback gated, not imported by the normal application, and absent from the standard production build. It makes no API requests. All callbacks are explicitly fictional local simulations. Refresh resets data. The toolbar offers lifecycle, access, screen and failure examples; query parameters include scenario, access, state, entryNote. Stock entry example starts Ready so the transition can be reviewed. It is not a backend implementation or proof of authoritative permissions/impact checks.
+
+History, comments, attachments, lifecycle forms and missing document destinations are local review compositions; existing production components remain on the normal route. Local document selection does not upload. Email Send queues a fictional row only. Customs clearing is explicitly listed before confirmation; real coverage-resolution choices still require FRO-356. The local review demonstrates compatible impacts, not every possible backend conflict resolution.
+
+### Continuation verification
+
+45 test files / 181 tests passed. Build passed. Typecheck reports only the two pre-existing delivery-note test casts. New focused coverage includes independent Notes/row drafts, exact totals/copy whitelist, locked fields, stale Details confirmations, Escape cancellation, revoked disposition capability and email preparation/context invalidation. Browser checks include Notes errors/retention, draft navigation, customs clearing review, colli expansion, Greek400px and external-reader visibility. Backend authorization, concurrency, real email delivery and document workflows remain unverified. No production branch/commit/publication occurred.
